cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use urdf-usd-bridge in work you publish, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: "urdf-usd-bridge: a stability layer and cross-backend validator for URDF-derived OpenUSD robot assets"
abstract: >-
  urdf-usd-bridge inspects URDF-derived OpenUSD assets, reports what physics
  data they actually carry per namespace, and repairs the gaps -- drive gains,
  armature, inertia tensors and joint limits -- as non-destructive USD overlay
  layers, in each backend's own unit convention. It ships a cross-backend
  simulation harness that runs PhysX, Newton and MuJoCo Warp from one
  interpreter, so every tuning constant it uses is either measured or labelled
  unmeasured. On 14 robots across 3 backends, repair improved hold-pose drift
  in 35 of 84 cells and worsened it in none, and 19 runs that diverged on
  converter output converged after repair.
type: software
authors:
